TITLE:: DeleteCommand
SUMMARY:: Command that deletes selected piano-roll notes.
CATEGORIES:: Commands
RELATED:: Classes/Command, Classes/Parameter, Classes/CommandPrompt, Classes/PianoRoll, Classes/PianoRollNote

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::DeleteCommand:: is a LINK::Classes/Command:: named CODE::delete:: that deletes every note in CODE::selectedNotes::. LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: supplies the notes through LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt#-ambientParameters:: as CODE::selectedNotes::, so the user does not type an argument. After the CODE::delete:: chip is committed, LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt:: treats the command as satisfied. Press Return to execute. With the piano-roll note area focused, the Delete key runs this command on the selected notes.

Each note that responds to CODE::delete:: is deleted. LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote#-delete:: removes the note view and runs the note's delete callback, which drops the note from the roll and updates the embedded LINK::Classes/RealTimePlayer:: sequence. An empty selection is a no-op. A note that is already deleted is left out of the undo step.

LINK::#-beforeImage:: stores the same amplitude snapshot LINK::Classes/AmpCommand:: stores, including CODE::\deleted:: false. LINK::#-restore:: writes that snapshot back through LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote#-restoreAmplitudeImage::, which is the same membership restore as amplitude CODE::0::. Undo puts the note back in the roll and creates its view again. Redo deletes it again.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a new TELETYPE::DeleteCommand::. Takes no arguments; deletion is applied by LINK::#-execute::.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::DeleteCommand:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: afterImage
The amplitude snapshot of each note in the before-image, after LINK::#-execute::. CODE::\deleted:: is true.

ARGUMENT:: args
The same arguments dictionary passed to LINK::#-execute::.

ARGUMENT:: before
The LINK::Classes/IdentityDictionary:: returned by LINK::#-beforeImage::.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/IdentityDictionary:: from note to its LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote#-amplitudeImage::, or CODE::nil:: when CODE::before:: is empty.

METHOD:: beforeImage
The amplitude snapshot of each selected note that is still in the roll. A note that is already deleted is left out.

ARGUMENT:: args
The same arguments dictionary about to be passed to LINK::#-execute::.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/IdentityDictionary:: from note to its LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote#-amplitudeImage::, or CODE::nil:: when every selected note is already deleted.

METHOD:: execute
Deletes each note in CODE::\selectedNotes:: that responds to CODE::delete::.

ARGUMENT:: args
A LINK::Classes/Dictionary:: or LINK::Classes/Event:: with CODE::\selectedNotes:: (an LINK::Classes/Array:: of notes that respond to CODE::delete::). A missing or empty array deletes nothing.

METHOD:: restore
Writes each snapshot back through LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote#-restoreAmplitudeImage::. A snapshot with CODE::\deleted:: false puts the note back. A snapshot with CODE::\deleted:: true deletes it.

ARGUMENT:: image
An LINK::Classes/IdentityDictionary:: from note to an amplitude snapshot, or CODE::nil::.

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
(
var notes = [
	PianoRollNote(0, 60, 100,
		viewFunc: { View() },
		selectFunc: {},
		deselectFunc: {},
		paintFunc: {},
		moveFunc: {},
		deleteFunc: { |note| ("deleted " ++ note.noteNumber).postln }
	),
	PianoRollNote(1, 64, 100,
		viewFunc: { View() },
		selectFunc: {},
		deselectFunc: {},
		paintFunc: {},
		moveFunc: {},
		deleteFunc: { |note| ("deleted " ++ note.noteNumber).postln }
	)
];
notes.do({ |note| note.stop(note.startTime + 1.0) });
DeleteCommand.new.execute((selectedNotes: notes));
)
::

PRIVATE:: prEachNote
